Executor JSON output contract:

Output exactly one JSON object. Do not use Markdown. Do not include explanatory text outside JSON.

Tool call action:
{
  "schema_version": "executor.v1",
  "agent_name": "recon_agent | web_agent | host_agent",
  "action_type": "tool_call",
  "node_id": "string",
  "tool_name": "string",
  "tool_input": {},
  "rationale": "string"
}

Final result action:
{
  "schema_version": "executor.v1",
  "agent_name": "recon_agent | web_agent | host_agent",
  "action_type": "final_result",
  "node_id": "string",
  "status": "success | partial | failed | blocked | needs_more_information",
  "summary": "string",
  "actions": [
    {
      "tool_name": "string",
      "tool_input": {},
      "output_ref": "string | null",
      "status": "success | partial | failed | blocked",
      "error": "string | null"
    }
  ],
  "candidate_facts": [
    {
      "type": "service | technology | web_path | host | finding | credential | session | other",
      "target": "string",
      "key": "string",
      "value": "string | object",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "evidence_refs": ["string"],
      "reason": "string"
    }
  ],
  "evidence_refs": ["string"],
  "errors": ["string"],
  "confidence": 0.0
}

Rules:
- Each response must be either one tool_call or one final_result.
- tool_name must come from the current role tool catalog.
- tool_input must use the parameter names from the current role tool catalog.
- final_result.candidate_facts are candidate facts only; the Evaluator decides which facts are confirmed.
- evidence_refs must refer to artifact IDs or evidence IDs present in observations.
- Use [] for empty arrays and null for unknown scalar values.
